    "result": "Perfect! The fix is working correctly:\n- \u2705 With `--ci` flag: Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are created\n- \u2705 Without `--ci` flag: Only `FRAI-SPEC.md` is created\n\nThe bug has been fixed! The issue was that the frai CLI's `gate` command wasn't passing through unknown options to the underlying frai-gate CLI. The solution was to extract all arguments from `process.argv` after the `gate` keyword and pass them directly to the spawned gate CLI, ensuring all flags and arguments are preserved.\n\n**Summary of changes:**\n- Modified `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` in the `gate` command's action handler to pass all arguments after `gate` to the frai-gate CLI by extracting them from `process.argv`\n- Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Verified the fix works correctly with both `--ci` and without the flag",
